@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2123 = private unnamed_addr constant [650 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of a `return` statement with no explicit value,\0Afor functions that return non-`None` values elsewhere.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIncluding a `return` statement with no explicit value can cause confusion\0Awhen other `return` statements in the function return non-`None` values.\0APython implicitly assumes return `None` if no other return value is present.\0AAdding an explicit `return None` can make the code more readable by clarifying\0Aintent.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return\0A    return 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return None\0A    return 1\0A```\0A", align 1
