@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2126 = private unnamed_addr constant [588 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for missing explicit `return` statements at the end of functions\0Athat can return non-`None` values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe lack of an explicit `return` statement at the end of a function that\0Acan return non-`None` values can cause confusion. Python implicitly returns\0A`None` if no other return value is present. Adding an explicit\0A`return None` can make the code more readable by clarifying intent.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo(bar):\0A    if not bar:\0A        return 1\0A    return None\0A```\0A", align 1
