@anon.b4276b7b39cc559116fc5d29527aa342.2236 = private unnamed_addr constant [1043 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function definitions that include too many positional arguments.\0A\0ABy default, this rule allows up to five arguments, as configured by the\0A[`lint.pylint.max-positional-args`] option.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFunctions with many arguments are harder to understand, maintain, and call.\0AThis is especially true for functions with many positional arguments, as\0Aproviding arguments positionally is more error-prone and less clear to\0Areaders than providing arguments by name.\0A\0AConsider refactoring functions with many arguments into smaller functions\0Awith fewer arguments, using objects to group related arguments, or migrating to\0A[keyword-only arguments](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html#special-parameters).\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Adef plot(x, y, z, color, mark, add_trendline): ...\0A\0A\0Aplot(1, 2, 3, \22r\22, \22*\22, True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef plot(x, y, z, *, color, mark, add_trendline): ...\0A\0A\0Aplot(1, 2, 3, color=\22r\22, mark=\22*\22, add_trendline=True)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pylint.max-positional-args`\0A", align 1
